From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 22:56:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: open-intent lookup also matches submitting and held

has_open_strategy_intent matched queued and submitted only, so an intent the
consumer had claimed (submitting) or paused (held) was not seen as open by the
protective-exit check during a kill cooldown. Match every in-flight status.

Verified (Python 3.11.15, cloud clone): tests/test_kill_gate_protective_exit.py
=> 19 passed; the submitting and held cases fail before the change.

HIGH risk: READY_FOR_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW. Not pushed, not deployed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011p3WBrLHso7qjbJYsguxAY
---
 docs/work_log/review_stabilized_work_log.md | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 storage/intent_queue_sqlite.py              |  2 +-
 tests/test_kill_gate_protective_exit.py     | 21 +++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 42 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/docs/work_log/review_stabilized_work_log.md b/docs/work_log/review_stabilized_work_log.md
index ac4ae043..c7c936ea 100644
--- a/docs/work_log/review_stabilized_work_log.md
+++ b/docs/work_log/review_stabilized_work_log.md
@@ -1,5 +1,25 @@
 # Review Stabilized Work Log
 
+## 2026-10-02 - Open-intent lookup covers submitting and held
+
+- ENGINEER (Claude, separate thread), chosen by the operator from the open
+  findings. Separate change, separate review.
+- Defect: the accepted `IntentQueueSQLite.has_open_strategy_intent` lookup
+  matched `queued` and `submitted` only. The paper queue also moves an intent
+  through `submitting` (claimed, not yet submitted) and `held`; in those states
+  the protective-exit check during a kill cooldown saw no open intent.
+- Change: the query matches queued, submitting, submitted and held. One line
+  of SQL. Its only caller is the protective-exit check, which becomes more
+  conservative: an exit is not let through the cooldown while an order for the
+  symbol is in any in-flight state.
+- Not changed: the inherited open-intent check on the normal emission path,
+  which reads the newest 200 intents and matches queued and submitted only.
+- VERIFIED_ENV (cloud clone, Python 3.11.15): tests/test_kill_gate_protective_
+  exit.py => 19 passed; the submitting and held cases fail before the change.
+- UNVERIFIED: Python 3.12, CI, two-process timing with the intent consumer.
+  HIGH risk (changes human-accepted code). Not pushed, not deployed.
+  READY_FOR_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW.
+
 ## 2026-10-02 - Count pending entries toward the concurrent-position limit
 
 - ENGINEER (Claude, separate thread). Follows the pending-order exposure probe
diff --git a/storage/intent_queue_sqlite.py b/storage/intent_queue_sqlite.py
index c126f117..f223cc3b 100644
--- a/storage/intent_queue_sqlite.py
+++ b/storage/intent_queue_sqlite.py
@@ -223,7 +223,7 @@ class IntentQueueSQLite:
         try:
             return con.execute(
                 "SELECT 1 FROM trade_intents WHERE source='strategy' AND symbol=? "
-                "AND status IN ('queued', 'submitted') LIMIT 1",
+                "AND status IN ('queued', 'submitting', 'submitted', 'held') LIMIT 1",
                 (str(symbol),),
             ).fetchone() is not None
         finally:
diff --git a/tests/test_kill_gate_protective_exit.py b/tests/test_kill_gate_protective_exit.py
index ae2c902e..c4b628aa 100644
--- a/tests/test_kill_gate_protective_exit.py
+++ b/tests/test_kill_gate_protective_exit.py
@@ -191,3 +191,24 @@ def test_exit_blocked_by_open_or_unknown_intent_does_not_repeat_bookkeeping(monk
     assert state.get(f"loss_streak:{KEY}") in (None, "0")
     assert state.get(f"cum_pnl:{KEY}") in (None, "0", "0.0")
     assert state.get(f"kill_remaining:{KEY}") == "4"
+
+
+@pytest.mark.parametrize(
+    "status, is_open",
+    [("queued", True), ("submitting", True), ("submitted", True), ("held", True),
+     ("filled", False), ("canceled", False), ("rejected", False), ("error", False)],
+)
+def test_open_intent_lookup_covers_every_in_flight_status(monkeypatch, tmp_path, status, is_open):
+    from storage import intent_queue_sqlite as queue_module
+
+    path = tmp_path / "queue.sqlite"
+    with sqlite3.connect(path) as con:
+        con.execute("CREATE TABLE trade_intents (source TEXT, symbol TEXT, status TEXT, created_ts TEXT)")
+        con.execute(
+            "INSERT INTO trade_intents(source, symbol, status, created_ts) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?)",
+            ("strategy", "BTC/USD", status, "2026-10-01"),
+        )
+    monkeypatch.setattr(queue_module, "_connect", lambda: sqlite3.connect(path))
+    queue = object.__new__(queue_module.IntentQueueSQLite)
+
+    assert queue.has_open_strategy_intent("BTC/USD") is is_open
